  message: "Shipped via PR #197. Closes the Go grpc.py struct embedding traversal gap by wiring _link_go_methods_to_rpc_routes through the WI-halat _transitive_bases helper. link_grpc accepts existing_edges; the registry entrypoint threads ctx.edges through. 4 new property tests; 100% coverage. Per BVT discipline: tagging awaits_bakeoff_validation + for_uat_bakeoff (UAT cycle: a Go gRPC ttrpc / CSI codebase like containerd or kata-containers protects this verdict)."  # d178
- op: discuss  # 901d
  at: '2026-05-08T23:48:55Z'  # 901d
  by: agent  # 901d
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 901d
  clock: 4  # 901d
  nonce: 901d  # 901d
  message: "UAT round 07 of hg-uat-v4.1.0 (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/bakeoff_artifacts/hg-uat-v4.1.0/lab-notebook/round-07-WI-pogus-go-grpc-ttrpc-transitive/) verdict: inconclusive. containerd uses only direct (1-hop) embedding of Unimplemented*Server; zero transitive embedding chains exist in tree. Per plan caveat, this triggers the inconclusive verdict — the transitive aspect of WI-pogus's fix is untestable on containerd.\n\nTag retained per inconclusive lifecycle. Two follow-up actions documented:\n\n(1) Re-route to kata-containers in a future UAT round to actually exercise the transitive walk. SHOULD WAIT for BUG-05 (WI-kunoz-mogik-tafam-gahik-zorin-zosiv-dozir-tovil, P1 todo_hard) to ship first. Round 07 surfaced BUG-05 as an independent grpc-linker correctness issue: the linker's name-precondition gate diverts struct named 'service' (lowercase, no Service/Server suffix) to a short-name-fallback path, mis-attributing 7 service families in containerd. Re-running on kata-containers without fixing BUG-05 would produce direct-embedding-tier misresolutions that poison honest assessment of the transitive fix.\n\n(2) After BUG-05 ships and Round 07 is re-routed to kata-containers (or another Go ttrpc target with multi-level UnimplementedFooServer embedding), the verdict on WI-pogus's transitive walk becomes assessable. Until then this item stays tagged.\n\nThe transitive-walk infrastructure WI-pogus added (collect_transitive_base_names in linkers/_transitive_bases.py, threaded into grpc.py via existing_edges) ships correctly and is exercised by the Python framework-dispatch linkers via WI-halat's path. Only the Go grpc-linker leg is awaiting target-availability + BUG-05 closure for empirical validation."  # 901d
